    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44410" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sinti</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sintii</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Macedonia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Heraclea ex Sintiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					42, 51, 7</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sintĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the</i> Sintii, <i>Sintian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Heraclea Sintica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 10, 17, § 35</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">or, Sintice Heraclea,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					45, 29, 6</span></i>
			 and 7.</div>
